  "body": {
    "id": "prop:local-ambiguity",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For any tangent-rich completion \\(Q\\) of \\(P\\), the compatible target set contains a relatively open neighborhood of \\(\\theta(Q)\\) in \\(\\theta(Q)+R_0\\ker(A_P)\\), and this affine space has dimension \\(\\nu(P)\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "Q",
      "P",
      "theta",
      "R_0",
      "A_P",
      "nu_P"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:signed-cell-lift",
      "ass:outcome-support-tangent"
    ],
    "justification": "The dimension \\(\\nu(P)\\) quantifies the locally attainable causal ambiguity rather than reporting only a binary identification verdict.",
    "gap": "Existing bridge-fiber statements do not establish a neighborhood of support-feasible causal targets.",
    "consumer": "Designers can measure how many target-relevant directions a proposed data addition removes.",
    "proof_tex": "Write \\(\\nu=\\nu(P)=\\dim(R_0\\ker A_P)\\), using the rank identity in the exact-nullity theorem.  For \\(\\nu=0\\), the singleton \\(\\{\\theta(Q)\\}\\) is relatively open in its zero-dimensional affine space.  Suppose \\(\\nu>0\\).  Choose \\(h_1,\\ldots,h_\\nu\\in\\ker(A_P)\\) so that \\(R_0h_1,\\ldots,R_0h_\\nu\\) is a basis of \\(R_0\\ker(A_P)\\), and let \\(\\Delta_j\\) be the carrier-supported signed-cell array constructed from \\(h_j\\).  Each step \\(h\\mapsto r^h\\mapsto d^h\\mapsto\\Delta^h\\) is linear, so the array associated with \\(\\sum_jt_jh_j\\) is \\(\\sum_jt_j\\Delta_j\\).\n\nOn the finite positive support set define\n\\[\nM=\\max_{s,x,u,w,y:\\,K_{s,x,u,w}(y)>0}\n\\frac{\\sum_{j=1}^{\\nu}|\\Delta_{j,s,x,u,w}(y)|}{K_{s,x,u,w}(y)}.\n\\tag{1}\n\\]\nFiniteness and positivity make \\(M<\\infty\\).  Moreover \\(M>0\\): if every \\(\\Delta_j\\) were zero, then the target-population part of the carrier construction would give \\(r^{h_j}_a(x,u)=0\\) for all \\(a,x,u\\), and hence \\(R_0h_j=0\\), contradicting the basis choice.  If \\(\\lVert t\\rVert_\\infty<M^{-1}\\), then on each positive atom\n\\[\n\\left|\\sum_jt_j\\Delta_{j,s,x,u,w}(y)\\right|\n\\le\\lVert t\\rVert_\\infty\\sum_j|\\Delta_{j,s,x,u,w}(y)|\n<K_{s,x,u,w}(y).\n\\tag{2}\n\\]\nThe linear preservation equations in the signed-cell proof therefore show that \\(K+\\sum_jt_j\\Delta_j\\) defines a compatible law with observed law \\(P\\) and target\n\\[\n\\theta(Q)+\\sum_{j=1}^{\\nu}t_jR_0h_j.\n\\tag{3}\n\\]\nAs \\(t\\) ranges over the open cube in (2), (3) is a relatively open neighborhood of \\(\\theta(Q)\\) in \\(\\theta(Q)+R_0\\ker(A_P)\\).  Its dimension is \\(\\nu(P)\\) by (1) of the exact-nullity proof.",
